@flexiarg apparatus/recorded-failures-before-live-runs
@title The Route Is Proved On Recorded Failures Before A Live Run Is Bought
@keywords replay, fixtures, pinned-records, fake-seats, live-budget, verification-order, clicks
@audience apparatus builders, campaign stewards, futon developers
@tone technical
@style pattern
@grade principle
@status proposed (2026-10-19; authored by claude-5 after the advice was given twice to codex-68 — claude-4 on 2026-10-18 for the WM click-3 production-boundary replay, claude-5 on 2026-10-19 for the META self-heal route; promotion gate: the self-heal replay harness exists and its first live click matches it)
@why apparatus/replayable-not-precious
@see-also apparatus/done-is-observed-running apparatus/new-failure-class-is-a-design-defect apparatus/special-flow-is-a-path-not-a-trail-of-exceptions
@violation-signature A live run is requested to "see whether the fix holds"; each live run reaches one gate further than the last; a budget of runs is exhausted with no end-to-end completion; the recorded failures of previous runs are not used as test inputs.
! conclusion: A multi-stage route is proved end to end on recorded failures and fake participants before a live run is spent on it; the live run then confirms a trace shape the harness has already produced, and never discovers the route.

  + context: An apparatus runs a costly unit of work (a WM click, a campaign slice, a deployment) whose failures are recorded as pinned bytes, and the route under repair spans several stages and several participants.

  + IF:
    A route has been patched after a live failure, and the question is whether the next live run will complete it.

  + HOWEVER:
    The live run is the only executor anyone has built, so it becomes the test. Each run reaches the next gate, fails there in a new way, and the fix for that gate is written against one run's evidence. Ten runs later the route is still unproved, the run budget is gone, and the patches form a trail of local widenings. The live run cannot tell a design defect from a missing case because it exercises one path per outing.

  + THEN:
    Build the proof in this order, and only then ask for a live run.
    1. A fixture corpus: every recorded failure from the campaign, as pinned bytes, in a table-driven test that states what each one must classify as.
    2. A pure state machine for the route with property tests over its transitions.
    3. Fake participants: register the seats the route dispatches to (author, reviewer, repair reviewer) as local functions in a test registry that return canned results on a throwaway branch, and run the whole route in its own process with a failure injected at each stage in turn.
    4. A replay of one real recorded run from its inputs, with the trace diffed against the harness trace.
    5. One live run, with scheduling still disarmed, whose trace is compared to the replay's.
    The fake participants prove the route's shape, not the participants' competence; the live run proves the latter, and only after the shape is proved.

  + BECAUSE:
    Live runs are the scarce resource and the slowest signal: one gate per outing, at the cost of a budget unit, with the operator waiting. Recorded failures are free, exact, and already pinned, so a harness built on them exercises every stage per second instead of one stage per click. Separating the shape of the route from the competence of its participants also makes the first live failure attributable: a shape failure is a harness gap, a competence failure is the seat's.

    + evidence: WM META self-heal, 2026-10-19: a five-click campaign reached one gate per click (loop-node gate, construction fold, injury persistence, author dispatch, injury classification) and ended at 106/106 budget with no end-to-end repair; futon2 97eab2ee8, fa43dd757, 5a5b421bc, 42bfb4bb5, 95145f093 are the five single-gate patches. Earlier, claude-4's 2026-10-18 review of the WM readiness campaign to codex-68 (Agency job invoke-1792360592468-16667-7ab8a8bf) named the click-3 production-boundary replay as the first completion of the post-selection route, and asked for replay evidence before further live work.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    - When the self-heal harness lands, record here whether its first live click matched the replay trace; that is the promotion evidence.
    - Name the fixture corpus location for WM clicks so later campaigns start from it rather than from a fresh live run.
